    "body": "> which may run as a Web extension or as a separate App depending on the platform\r\n\r\nIn this case, modifying this spec seems incorrect, as this spec is what allows websites to intercept the scheme and *prevent* extensions or external applications from handling it. If you want an extension or external app to handle a scheme, those aren't governed by the HTML Standard.",
